  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `rest_pocket_with_relief` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/rest2d.rs`) keeps a planned corner relief when its start is in the rest center area grown by 0.01 mm (`RELIEF_START_TOL`).\n- Each relief that the rest pass does not keep now gives a toolpath note: `corner relief at (x, y) is not cut: the rest area does not reach that corner`.\n- The decision record is `docs/decisions/3146-rest-relief-boundary.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe old filter was `.filter(|r| plan.center.contains(r.start))`. Each relief start is a vertex of the pocket's own center area. Where the rest area touches a corner, that vertex is on the boundary of the rest center area. `Region::contains` on a boundary point gives `true` or `false` by rounding. On a sharp 30 x 30 mm pocket, the rest pass cut 1 of 4 dogbones and gave no note.\n\nThe start stays a legal tool position. It is always on the plain pocket's own center area, so the tolerance cannot move the tool past a wall.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew file `crates/motion/tests/rest_corner_relief.rs`:\n\n- `rest_pass_cuts_all_four_dogbones_of_a_sharp_square_pocket`: the 30 x 30 mm pocket, 6 mm tool, previous tool 16 mm, `CornerReliefKind::Dogbone`. Each of the 4 dogbone ends is cut at the floor, for Waterline, OffsetRings and Zigzag. No relief note.\n  - Red before the fix: `Waterline: rest pass missed dogbone ends [(27.88, 27.88), (2.12, 27.88), (27.88, 2.12)]`.\n- `rest_pass_notes_a_forced_relief_the_rest_area_does_not_reach`: an override forces a dogbone on a 176 deg corner. The previous tool leaves only a film there, so the rest area does not reach it. The pass does not cut it, and a note names it.\n\nMutation checks:\n\n- Old `rest2d.rs` from `upstream/main`: both pins red.\n- The fix with a bare `plan.center.contains` (no tolerance): the count pin red, at line 72.\n- Fix restored: both pins green.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green (motion lib, `rest_corner_relief`, `rest_zigzag`, `rest2d`, app `rest_pocket`). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The shared spur emitter (`inject_relief_spurs`) can still skip a kept relief without a note when no pass vertex links to it. That code is shared with the plain pocket and is not changed here.\n- Heavy lanes were not run.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #2822 and #2890 change other parts of `rest2d.rs` (`rest_pocket` / `emit_rest`). They do not contain the relief filter. This PR touches the same file, different lines; whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: A 2D Pocket rest pass with corner reliefs now cuts the relief at every inside corner that the rest area touches, and notes a relief that it does not cut.\n\nFixes #3146\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
